{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAFp3MTezBkqYo8G4byf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The recovery middleware no longer treats `panic(http.ErrAbortHandler)` as a crash. The full package test suite passes, including a new test for this case.\n\nBefore, it logged a full panic stack trace and called the 500 handler. That panic is the standard way to abort a response, and `httputil.ReverseProxy` uses it. Now, in `recovery.go`:\n- **No logging:** nothing is written, which matches how `net/http` itself treats this panic.\n- **No write to the client:** it takes the same path as the broken-pipe case, recording the error with `c.Error` and calling `c.Abort()`.\n\nThe new test, `TestPanicWithAbortHandler` in `recovery_test.go`, checks that the status code set before the panic is kept and nothing is logged.\n\nUnlike broken pipes, which still log a short line, this case is fully silent. The middleware also catches the panic rather than re-panicking, so `net/http` never sees it and doesn't cut the connection itself. I haven't committed anything; HEAD is detached, so say if you want a branch and a commit with that message."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":430,"cache_read_input_tokens":34675,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":430,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f469dca-8880-436d-a205-e8bdc8df29aa","uuid":"d6f5cb82-699d-4f12-ba3d-c6bd872bef26","timestamp":"2026-10-18T19:29:32.698Z","request_id":"req_011CgAFp39Z7bQg2e6fg4Q22"}
