`net/http` itself treats this panic.\n- **No write to the client:** it takes the same path as the broken-pipe case, recording the error with `c.Error` and calling `c.Abort()`.\n\nThe new test, `TestPanicWithAbortHandler` in `recovery_test.go`, checks that the status code set before the panic is kept and nothing is logged.\n\nUnlike broken pipes, which still log a short line, this case is fully silent. The middleware also catches the panic rather than re-panicking, so `net/http` never sees it and doesn't cut the connection itself. I haven't committed anything; HEAD is detached, so say if you want a branch and a commit with that message.","ttft_ms":2106,"type":"result","duration_ms":31222,"uuid":"e511f1b2-9dbb-4600-987e-f1c3cd70ddb4","ttft_stream_ms":1703,"time_to_request_ms":138,"first_content_frame_ms":1703,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
